{
  "format": "bgsim.model",
  "language": "0.1.0",
  "name": "balancer",
  "$comment": "Gravity ON variant: the planar reaction-wheel balancer. GroundPlanar -> Pivot (Revolute2DCompliant, compliant pivot kt = 1e9 N/m, bt = 5e3 N s/m) -> LinkB (FixedJoint2D to the body centre of mass 0.3 m up, body frame x along the link) -> BodyJ (1-junction) with Body (RigidBody2D: m = 1.5 kg, J = 0.02) and WheelJ (Revolute2DCompliant, its axis 0.2 m further along the body frame, i.e. 0.5 m above the pivot) -> Wheel (RigidBody2D: m = 0.4 kg, J = 0.002, its centre on the axis). Motor: MSe(tau) on the wheel drive. Balancer: 1 ms PD on the body angle with gravity feedforward (G = 6.3765 sin theta), tau limit 1.5 N m. The body starts 0.01 rad off upright, recovers, and follows a 0.012 rad reference pulse from 0.5 s to 1.5 s; the wheel spins up during the tilt and spins down again when the body returns.",
